\section{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}

\textbf{C2 scope.} C2 is preregistered as ROME-only. Both validated cells preserve
damage rank under INT8 and edited-layer NF4; full-model NF4 preservation is supported
at Llama-3.2-1B L12 but fails at Llama-3.2-3B L24. MEMIT and AlphaEdit are excluded by
scope, not by their observed FP32 statistic. The C2 number is the flattened-grid
rank (legacy sensitivity); the operational edit-level signed-mean rank is
reported in Table~\ref{tab:multilevel}. Extrapolation beyond these arm--cell combinations is not warranted.

\textbf{Track 1 is isolated per-edit.} Track 1 measures the effect of quantizing a
single edit's MLP down-projection in isolation, via the bitsandbytes codec
round-trip. Track 2 (PENDING) measures the deployment-realistic protocol of
installing all 200 edits then quantizing the whole model; the present paper does
not measure Track-2 batch deployment, and does not conflate the codec round-trip
with packed deployment inference.

\textbf{Track 1.5 is an honest SKIP.} GPTQ and AWQ are not installed under the
project's ask-first install rule. The frozen-scale codec utility raises
\texttt{NotImplementedError} for these kernels. The kernel choice matters for the
bin-width statistic and per-block outlier handling; results under GPTQ/AWQ could
differ.

\textbf{Bin-width denominator provenance.} The reported $F_{\mathrm{above}}$ and median
$|\Delta W|/b$ use the legacy/local-gap denominator $b=\mathrm{absmax}_{\mathrm{block}}\,\mathrm{local\_gap}(w/\mathrm{absmax}_{\mathrm{block}})$ with blocksize 64. They are sensitivity proxies only; the amended channel-scale $\times$ NF4 minimum-gap K3 axis remains pending a targeted rerun. No directionality is claimed from the legacy values. The denominator/F1 corrections applied in the manuscript (e.g.\ the Qwen absolute mean ESR in Table~\ref{tab:absolutes}) follow the preregistration DRAFT's recorded entries on the bin-width denominator and the F1 definition; the manuscript does not classify them as pre- vs.\ post-data, since the DRAFT was never ratified as active and the preregistration document's mtimes fall after several real cells. The threshold quantities that adjudicate C1/C2 are the prospectively specified values in the design document and are not changed by these corrections.

\textbf{INT8 has no bin-width axis (threshold = 0).} Real bitsandbytes INT8 uses
vectorwise quantization with an outlier dimension; this paper does not decompose
the INT8 path into an outlier + a bin-width axis, so INT8 has no adjudicated
outlier-decomposed statistic. INT8's $F_{\mathrm{above}}$/median-ratio columns
in Table~\ref{tab:c3} are reported for completeness and are not used for
directionality. The reconstruction-gap ratio $r_{\mathrm{func}} / r_{\mathrm{param}}$
is computed consistently across the evaluated kernels and is descriptive
evidence, not a load-bearing substitute for amended K3 adjudication.

\textbf{Qwen-2.5-1.5B L21 is a degeneracy datapoint.} The FP32 within-probe law does
not clear the gate at this layer; the cell is included for completeness but does not
gate any claim. The Qwen absolute mean ESR is reported alongside the conditional
survival so that the absolute floor of the protocol is visible (Table~\ref{tab:absolutes}).

\textbf{Preregistration DRAFT and omitted cells.} The preregistration document
for this study was prepared as a DRAFT and was not ratified as active before any
cell ran; the cell runs proceeded under the project's house pre-specification
convention. The Llama-3.1-8B cell from the DRAFT grid was omitted from this
submission: its FP32 within-probe law is dead at the tested layer, so it would
not have gated any claim, and including it would not change any reported
PASS/FAIL.

