\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Knowledge-edit effects can survive real INT8 and NF4 quantization, but the amended
bin-width concentration axis remains unadjudicated pending a targeted rerun. The
preregistered ROME efficacy threshold passes on Llama-3.2-1B and Qwen-2.5-1.5B; the
stronger editor-ordering prediction holds on Llama-1B but fails on Qwen. ROME edits at
Llama-3.2-1B L12 retain both efficacy (\pPrimarynfFourdqFullModelEsrSurv{}) and
damage-rank survival (\pPrimarynfFourdqFullModelRankSurv{}) at 4-bit full-model under
real bitsandbytes kernels; the second validated-law cell, Llama-3.2-3B L24, retains
efficacy (\pSecondnfFourdqFullModelEsrSurv{}) but its damage-rank survival falls to
\pSecondnfFourdqFullModelRankSurv{} below the specified \pRankSurvFourThreshold{}
threshold, narrowing the phenomenon to preservation under INT8 and edited-layer NF4
across both validated ROME cells, with full-model NF4 preservation supported at
Llama-3.2-1B L12 but not Llama-3.2-3B L24. The C2 number is the flattened-grid rank
(legacy sensitivity); the operational edit-level signed-mean rank from the
v1.2.1 repair artefact (Table~\ref{tab:multilevel}) is near-unity on both
validated-law ROME cells (Llama-3.2-1B L12 \pPriFNFMSignPt{}
CI95 [\pPriFNFMSignLo{},\,\pPriFNFMSignHi{}]; Llama-3.2-3B L24
\pSecFNFMSignPt{} CI95 [\pSecFNFMSignLo{},\,\pSecFNFMSignHi{}]). The C2
gate is the flattened-grid rank and the operational edit-level signed-mean
rank estimates a different (per-edit-pooled) ordering; the two statistics
can disagree numerically. On the operational edit-level axis the ranking
survives at 4-bit full-model on both validated ROME cells.
Qwen-2.5-1.5B L21 NF4 full-model is reported separately: the flat rank is
\pQwenFNFMFlat{}, the within-probe rank is \pQwenFNFMWithin{}, and the
edit-level signed-mean point is \pQwenFNFMSignPt{} with CI95
[\pQwenFNFMSignLo{},\,\pQwenFNFMSignHi{}] --- a wide CI driven by the low
absolute-ESR floor (CI95 [\pQwenFNFMAbsEsrLo{},\,\pQwenFNFMAbsEsrHi{}] width
\pQwenAbsEsrWidth{}). We do not claim a deployer-relevant survival on Qwen.
The legacy/local-gap sensitivity readout is not an adjudication of the amended concentration axis:
median $|\Delta W|/b$ sits below the unit threshold on Llama-3.2-1B L12 ROME
(\pPrimaryNfFourDqMedianRatio{}) and on Llama-3.2-3B L24 ROME
(\pSecondNfFourDqMedianRatio{}); $F_{\mathrm{above}}$ is below 1\% on both. INT8
has no outlier-decomposed bin-width axis in this paper's accounting (threshold = 0).
The descriptive reconstruction-gap signature appears in every C3 block:
$r_{\mathrm{func}} < r_{\mathrm{param}}$ throughout (18/18 scheme blocks), with
median $r_{\mathrm{func}}/r_{\mathrm{param}} \approx 5.7 \times 10^{-3}$ at INT8
and $\approx 5.9 \times 10^{-3}$ at NF4. Because the epsilon is implemented as
$\mathrm{Q}(W{+}d) - (W{+}d)$ rather than a quantized-update error, this signature
is descriptive of the total-rounding gap; it does not adjudicate the amended K3
axis and does not by itself imply a unique mechanism.

The reconciliation with absolute Strict-Edit-Locality F1 from prior work on
editing-under-compression (Hase et~al., arXiv 2407.06483) is left to the
deployed-kernel Track-2 bridge cell, which is PENDING driver completion. We do not
claim a measured replication of the F1 degradation here. The Qwen absolute mean
ESR (FP32 \pQwenRomeFpThirtyTwoAbsEsrPt{} / \pQwenMemitFpThirtyTwoAbsEsrPt{} / \pQwenAlphaFpThirtyTwoAbsEsrPt{}; NF4 full-model \pQwenRomeNfFourFMAbsEsrPt{} / \pQwenMemitNfFourFMAbsEsrPt{} / \pQwenAlphaNfFourFMAbsEsrPt{}) and the
conditional survival (NF4 full-model \pGridQOneRomeNfFourFMCond{} /
\pGridQOneMemitNfFourFMCond{} / \pGridQOneAlphaNfFourFMCond{}) are reported together
in Table~\ref{tab:absolutes}; the $n = 40$ generation checks show mean perplexity
rises of \pPplRisePctMin{}--\pPplRisePctMax{}\% from FP32-edited to NF4 full-model across cells.

